hooting in El Paso targeting  Mexicans members say they're prepared to  defend themselves do you feel the  this political climate that white  nationalists are emboldened to go after  minority groups and you need this  protection I do I like I said even  though I generalize it's not just crime  in our communities but it's also a white  nationalist I mean I do believe they are  emboldened and yes I want to be armed I  want to I'm not going down without a  fight  so I look at it that way and so by being  able to protect ourselves by training  properly and getting our practice in and  learning how to defend ourselves at  least we will be able to fight back if  we are attacked from white supremacy  white nationalist Nagas promotes the  Second Amendment and social justice but  Smith says he's aware of the dangers of  being black and legally armed in America  he pointed to the falando Castile case  in Minnesota where Castile who was  licensed to carry a gun was shot and  killed by a police officer during a 2016  traffic stop Naga immediately condemned  the shooting while Smith points out  other prominent gun rights groups like  the National Rifle Association did not  them not speaking up says more to us  than anything are you in agreement with  that I couldn't be silent tears came out  of Minds when I heard this brother got  shot if you're an organization and once  you get black folks to back you up  that's the best way speak out when you  see injustice don't sit there silently  like you don't know what's happening  because we're a very intelligent group  of folks the group is talking about  getting political in endorsing  candidates which could make them a  political force but they're not there  yet it's something they'll discuss at  their first national conference next  year for CBS this morning  Omar Villafranca Atlanta  that video the Castile shooting is still  very very painful and difficult to watch  and I thought he raised a really good  point you know we're speakin